# Bilbo, Thief in the Night: the attack trigger casts "an artifact, instant, or sorcery spell", and a creature spell is
# none of these. Bot2 bolts Bot1's Llanowar Elves on turn 2, so the only card in Bot1's graveyard is the Elves. On turn 5
# Bilbo attacks with a Forest untapped that could pay for the Elves ({G}): the trigger offers no card (so the
# question is not asked, and a default answer, which takes the first card on offer, would otherwise have cast it) and
# the Elves stay in the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Bilbo, Thief in the Night
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bilbo, Thief in the Night.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Bilbo, Thief in the Night)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield = Bilbo, Thief in the Night; Forest; Island
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = false
Bot2.Life = 18
